A single closed action may execute directly; otherwise finish and finalize a Plan before modifying project files.

While work is still open, native Goal continues the Todo list across turns. Keep exactly one `in_progress` at a time; update status with `todo_update` and an exact id. After every todo is terminal, call `todo_finish` with the actual outcome; do not finish while remaining work still depends on a running worker. `todo_read` only reads status.

Todos stay on this session. Agent spawn is a separate choice: write a self-contained prompt, and after the worker finishes verify the result and `todo_update` here. A running worker is a Lyra session, not an operating-system process. An empty process list, a clean git status, or files that are not on disk yet do not mean it has stopped. Do not look for it with ps, pgrep, or git status, and do not read its output to decide. While that worker is running, do not write or edit those files. Do the other work, or stop until notified.
